WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.167
-I'm so happy to see you
in person.

00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:03.334
-Me too.
-Welcome back.

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:04.334
-And all these beauties.
-And all these humans.

00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:06.033
Isn't that great?

00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:07.667
-Oh, my God.
-Doesn't that feel good?

00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:09.868
You're back.
You're back in New York.

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:11.434
You're back in the U.S.
-Yeah.

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:14.133
-You were just in Colombia.
-Yeah. Forever.

00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:16.634
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.
-Real time, three months.

00:00:16.634 --> 00:00:18.000
-Is that right?
-Yeah.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.234
We shot the first half
of the movie in Bogota,

00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:24.067
which is a big city.
Really fun. Great restaurants.

00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:26.334
And then we moved to the jungle

00:00:26.334 --> 00:00:28.367
for the second half
of the shoot.

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:29.434
-Yes.

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:32.667
-I lived in a house
with two birds.

00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:33.968
-You lived with them?

00:00:33.968 --> 00:00:38.300
-I lived in the birds' house
is another way to put it.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:41.534
-So the birds actually --
you met a bird that had a house?

00:00:41.534 --> 00:00:42.868
-"Could I stay here?"

00:00:42.868 --> 00:00:45.167
-Air Bird 'N' Bird.

00:00:45.167 --> 00:00:46.634
-Oh!

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:49.133
-Not bad, huh?
Not good, either.

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:50.968
But Airbnb.
-Yes.

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:52.200
-I'll work on it.
I'll work on it.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.567
-And the first couple of days
that I'm there,

00:00:54.567 --> 00:00:56.868
I drop my stuff, I'm working,
and in the middle of the night,

00:00:56.868 --> 00:00:59.033
I just heard a lot
of loud squawking.

00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:00.234
-Yeah.
-And I just sort of thought,

00:01:00.234 --> 00:01:02.067
"I'm in the jungle now."
-Yes.

00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:03.200
-Like, you know.
-Get used to it.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.667
This is what it is --
the jungle.

00:01:04.667 --> 00:01:08.467
-But by the third day I was
like, "This squawking is crazy.

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:10.567
It feels like
they're in the walls."

00:01:10.567 --> 00:01:14.033
And sure enough, I walk -- I do
some exploring around the house,

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:15.901
and I walk around the side of
the house and built

00:01:15.901 --> 00:01:20.567
into the house is a bird cage
with these two beautiful macaws,

00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:23.133
like these large,
colorful birds.

00:01:23.133 --> 00:01:24.133
-Ooh.

00:01:24.133 --> 00:01:26.534
-These birds are in a cage

00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:27.601
built into the side
of the house.

00:01:27.601 --> 00:01:30.033
I'm like, "What's happening?"
-Wow.

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:32.567
-"Was I supposed to be feeding
the birds?"

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:34.434
Like, it was sort of weird.
So, I find --

00:01:34.434 --> 00:01:36.601
The woman who works at the house
comes over and she says,

00:01:36.601 --> 00:01:40.467
"Well yes, the birds live here.
This is their house."

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:41.901
-Wow. I didn't know.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:44.133
-And I was, like,
"Let them out."

00:01:44.133 --> 00:01:45.767
-Yeah.
-Like, I'm going to be staying

00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:47.601
at the house for six weeks.
I'm like...

00:01:47.601 --> 00:01:49.200
-I'm staying at their house.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.300
-Yeah, and I've imprisoned them?
-Yeah.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:53.634
-So as she's opening the cage
to let them out, I'm like,

00:01:53.634 --> 00:01:55.501
"Well wait, are they dangerous
at all?"

00:01:55.501 --> 00:01:56.534
-Yeah, do they bite?

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:59.067
-And she's like,
"The blue one is old.

00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:01.634
He has one eye. He'll probably
stay away from you.

00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:03.667
But don't get too close
to the red one or it'll --"

00:02:03.667 --> 00:02:04.667
[ Clicking ]

00:02:04.667 --> 00:02:06.667
-Really?
-And so next thing I know,

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:09.801
this red one, he's up
in my business.

00:02:09.801 --> 00:02:12.968
This red one
wouldn't leave me alone.

00:02:12.968 --> 00:02:14.801
-You're having breakfast
with the red one there.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.400
-Can we get a tight shot?

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.100
This is how I feel about --

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:19.934
-Can we zoom in on Alison's face
there?

00:02:19.934 --> 00:02:22.801
-This is my feeling.

00:02:22.801 --> 00:02:25.734
What was at first really fun
and exciting.

00:02:25.734 --> 00:02:27.634
-Now he's your buddy everyday
and would just come

00:02:27.634 --> 00:02:28.667
and eat breakfast with you?

00:02:28.667 --> 00:02:30.200
-He was eating food
off my plate.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:31.267
Well, I'm not going to say no.

00:02:31.267 --> 00:02:32.501
I was like, "Please, please.

00:02:32.501 --> 00:02:34.367
I'm not supposed to get
too close to you."

00:02:34.367 --> 00:02:36.100
"Another mushroom, sir?"

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:38.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.367 --> 00:02:40.801
-I know you were in Colombia
filming

00:02:40.801 --> 00:02:42.567
with our friend, John Cena.

00:02:42.567 --> 00:02:44.133
-Yes, I was.

00:02:44.133 --> 00:02:45.400
-How was that?
He's just the most fun.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:46.434
-He's great. He's the best.

00:02:46.434 --> 00:02:47.501
-Have you worked with him
before?

00:02:47.501 --> 00:02:49.133
-No, I had never worked with him
before.

00:02:49.133 --> 00:02:51.000
-He's funny.
-But we bonded pretty quickly

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.133
over wrestling because...
-"Glow."

00:02:53.133 --> 00:02:54.901
-...I used worked on a show
called "Glow."

00:02:54.901 --> 00:02:57.100
-Hello. Yeah.
-That was about wrestling.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:01.033
And he used to work on
some wrestling show --

00:03:01.033 --> 00:03:02.701
-I can't think of it right now.
-I can't -- yeah.

00:03:02.701 --> 00:03:05.234
-I actually wanted to show this
because I follow you

00:03:05.234 --> 00:03:06.834
on the socials and you're great
to follow.

00:03:06.834 --> 00:03:08.868
-Thank you.
-And you posted this of you

00:03:08.868 --> 00:03:10.267
just working out at the gym.

00:03:10.267 --> 00:03:11.334
Just take a look at this.
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:13.400
-Watch Alison Brie.
This is insane.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:17.601
♪♪

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:19.467
-Come on. Come on.

00:03:19.467 --> 00:03:21.834
-Again, go.

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:24.367
Work. Work.

00:03:24.367 --> 00:03:25.501
-Now, here's why I love this.

00:03:25.501 --> 00:03:28.133
Not only is it impressive --

00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:30.467
not only is it impressive,
but I asked Alison, I go,

00:03:30.467 --> 00:03:32.968
"Oh, so you do a lot of
the stunts on -- in this movie?"

00:03:32.968 --> 00:03:35.200
And you go, "I don't really do
many stunts."

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.767
And I go, "What is that?
'Cause that's intense."

00:03:37.767 --> 00:03:40.300
-I was just gearing up to meet
John Cena.

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:42.167
-Yeah, you can't mess around.
-You know, I just wanted to --

00:03:42.167 --> 00:03:44.200
Yeah, most of the movie,
I'm just, like,

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.200
running near John Cena

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:49.133
and I wanted to be a baddie.

00:03:49.133 --> 00:03:51.334
-You are a baddie.
Yeah, you're fantastic.

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:54.267
-I had to gear up.

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:55.701
-All right.
Let's talk about "Roar."

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:56.868
-Yes.
-I'm very excited about this.

00:03:56.868 --> 00:03:58.767
It's an anthology series on
Apple TV Plus.

00:03:58.767 --> 00:04:00.767
Can you set up what's happening
in "Roar"?

00:04:00.767 --> 00:04:04.467
-Yes, it's eight episodes,
eight different stories

00:04:04.467 --> 00:04:09.133
and they're all a little
surreal, a little darkly comic

00:04:09.133 --> 00:04:12.701
feminist fables, if you will.
-Yes.

00:04:12.701 --> 00:04:15.801
-My episode is called "The woman
who solved her own murder."

00:04:15.801 --> 00:04:22.133
And it is a feminist take on
the classic male detective genre

00:04:22.133 --> 00:04:24.367
as seen through the eyes
of the woman who was murdered.

00:04:24.367 --> 00:04:25.400
-Yeah.
-Who I play.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:27.767
-So you're a ghost in --
-I'm a ghost.

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.133
-So I want to show everyone
a clip.

00:04:29.133 --> 00:04:30.667
Here's Alison Brie in "Roar."

00:04:30.667 --> 00:04:31.767
Take a look a this.

00:04:31.767 --> 00:04:33.501
-Patrol just dropped this off.

00:04:33.501 --> 00:04:35.434
They're sitting in a car about
half a mile away,

00:04:35.434 --> 00:04:36.968
registered to a --

00:04:36.968 --> 00:04:38.834
-Rebecca Moss.
-Rebecca Moss.

00:04:38.834 --> 00:04:41.567
-That's me.
-Wow, that's her.

00:04:41.567 --> 00:04:42.734
-Can we take a minute to
acknowledge

00:04:42.734 --> 00:04:43.767
the real tragedy here?

00:04:43.767 --> 00:04:45.167
I was clearly in my prime.

00:04:45.167 --> 00:04:46.667
-You think ID'ing a dead girl
is funny?

00:04:46.667 --> 00:04:48.567
-No. No.

00:04:48.567 --> 00:04:51.801
It' just -- who gets to blowout
and contours their face

00:04:51.801 --> 00:04:53.734
before a trip to the DMV?

00:04:53.734 --> 00:04:57.367
-Wow. You live with your license
photo a long time, Carol.

00:04:57.367 --> 00:04:58.901
-Okay.
-Unless you die.

00:04:58.901 --> 00:05:00.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:01.200
-You actually really do.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.801
Alison Brie, everybody.

00:05:02.801 --> 00:05:05.901
All episodes of "Roar"
are available April 15th

00:05:05.901 --> 00:05:07.534
on Apple TV Plus.

00:05:07.534 --> 00:05:08.801
Alison Brie!

